Sadly, I disagree with Jonathan about the twins choosing Lojban over
English to talk to Robin. I know of a boy in a household where both parents
used German and English daily, but the family lived in Germany, and the boy
spoke only German, although he could understand his mother just fine. He
very early gave up ever speaking English, even to her.

Despite this story, though, I have high hopes for Robin and his twins.

stevo


